      "track": {
        "artwork_url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-uWepS5qsLVlT-0-large.jpg",
        "caption": null,
        "commentable": true,
        "comment_count": 412,
        "created_at": "2014-08-12T14:44:39Z",
        "description": "I'm pleased to announce THE LIQUID AMBER EP. This single/EP serves as the opening salvo in what I hope is a long string of music, by myself and others, on my new imprint: LIQUID AMBER. There's two new songs, \"Ghost Town\" and \"Mob,\" and a nifty remix of \"Six Days\" by Machinedrum.\r\n\r\n\"Ghost Town\" is an ambitious ride through many of the micro-genres within the Future Bass umbrella that have inspired me recently, while \"Mob\" is an intentionally stripped-down, Cali-certified head-nodder. Both songs were written, programmed, and mixed by myself, and they represent the forward steps I feel I've taken as an engineer. The \"Six Days\" remix was something I asked Machinedrum to knock out as a tour weapon, and he crushed it (naturally), so I felt it deserved a proper release.\r\n\r\nI'm excited about this music and the new imprint, and I really appreciate everyone's time and consideration.\r\n\r\nDownload \"Ghost Town\" now on @edm at: bit.ly/DJS-GhostTown",
